1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Sigrid Jonsdatter'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1420 Sigrid Jonsdatter var muligens født i Buskerud. Foreldrene er ukjente. 
2 CONT * Sigrid giftet seg med  Dyre Erlendsson på Sørum,  sønn av Erlend Baardsson og Fru Erland Baardsen. De hadde sønnene Erlend, Sevald og Gunnar 
2 CONT * 1457 den 1. november "Fire Mænd kundgjöre, at Dyre Erlendssön og hans Hustru Sigrid Jonsdatter erkjendte at have solgt til Hr. Hartvig Krummedike 6 Öresbol Jord i Haga i Syltebygden i Haugs Sogn paa Eker og at have oppebaaret Be
2 CONC talingen"  Sammendrag .Diplomatarium Norvegicum (volumes I-XXI) b.VIII s.393
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigrun Jonsdatter Diplomatarium Norvegicum (volumes I-XXI) b.VIII s.393 Sammendrag: Fire Mænd kundgjöre, at Dyre Erlendssön og hans Hustru Sigrid Jonsdatter erkjendte at have solgt til Hr. Hartvig Krummedike 6 Öresbol Jord i Haga 
2 CONC i Syltebygden i Haugs Sogn paa Eker og at have oppebaaret Betalingen.Kilde: Efter Orig. p. Perg. i norske Rigsarkiv. Alle 4 Segl mangle.(Jfr. Dipl. Norv. VII. No. 478.) Nummer: 363.Dato: 1 Novbr. 1457. Sted: Sudrheim. Brevtekst (f
2 CONC ra den trykte utgaven):Allom monnom theim ssom tetthe breff s[ee] eller høyre sen-dher Gutorm Haraldhsson Kedel Torgardhsson Torleff Aulesson Hans Hermundhsson q. g. ok sine kunnikth gerendhe at mith varom a Ssudhreme ssom liger j
2 CONC  Ssteinssokn (a) Ringerike a Helgone møse dagh anno dominj mcdl sseptimo saghom ok høy[rdhom a a]t the heldo handhom ssaman aff eno halvo velboren man her Hartuik Krummedike ridher en aff anre halvo Dyree Erlendhsson ok Sigridh Io
2 CONC ns dotther egen kone hans medher thi skillordhe at fførnemdh Dyre kendis ffore oss at han haffdhe sselth adhernemdh her Hartuik vi aurebooll iordher j Hagha ssom ligger j Ssylltebygdh j Haugh ssokn a Eikiom ffriælssth ok heimalt f
2 CONC fore hvariom manne medher allom lutom ok lunindhom ssom ther til liger ok leget haver ffra fforne ok nye vtthen gardhz ok innen meder ia ok ssamtykt fførn(em)de Ssigridh ffra ssegh ok ssinom ervingiom vndher her Harttuik ok hans e
2 CONC rvingh[e] til euerdelege ege ok alz affredis. kendis the ok ath the hadhe vpboreth ffyrssthe peningh ok øffssthe effther thy ssom j kop tere kom. Thill thes mere visse ok b.VIII s.394 fforvaringh tha hengiom vi vare inssigle ffore
2 CONC  tethe bref ssomghiorth var dagh ok are ssom fføre siger.Tillegg: Bagpaa: bref om Haga i Syltobygd j Hawgx sokn a Eikiom.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.roysofting.com/Slekt/getperson.php?personID=I3967&tree=roy
2 CONT ----
2 CONT [http://www.oavesthagen.no/Mine_aner.htm Ole Arild Vesthagen: Mine aner] - nr. 82928<br/>
2 CONT Tore H. Vigerust: Dyre Sevaldssons ætt eller Lunner-ætten. [https://admin.slektogdata.no/sites/default/files/2019-08/1995-3.pdf Slekt og data 1995 Nr. 3] side 15<br/>
2 CONT Opprinnelsen ukjent, at hun er datter av Jon Seim er ikke nevnt i noen kilder
2 CONT
2 CONT Var hun født på Hvam Store gård på stedet Holter i Nes kommune i Viken fylke Norge?
2 CONT
2 CONT Eller på Seim gård på Oppstad på Skarnes i Sør-Odal kommune i Innlandet fylke Norge? Der hennes far kan ha vært bruker.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ⚠️ '''Note''': ''Recent research by Tore H. Vigerust and other genealogists has replaced earlier, unsubstantiated theories (such as the '''Seim''' or '''Hvam''' origin). Furthermore, while a connection to the high-noble Sudreim cl
2 CONC an has been proposed based on heraldic similarities, it remains undocumented due to the confirmed location of the 1457 transaction at Sudreim in '''Ringerike''', rather than the royal seat in Romerike. Tore H. Vigerust specificall
2 CONC y addressed these families in Slekt og Data 3/95 (p. 24-25), emphasizing the need for strict source-based evidence and rejecting "fantasy" lineages. The following lineage reflects the most accurate documentation currently availabl
2 CONC e.''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lineage and Biography''':
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigrid Jonsdatter was a member of the prominent Norwegian noble family known as the '''Holter''' clan. Modern genealogical reconstruction, supported by allodial (odel) rights and heraldic analysis, identifies her as the daughter o
2 CONC f the squire '''(væpner) Jon Holteson''' (mentioned 1391–1427) and the sister of the squires Amund and Gudbrand Jonsson.
2 CONT * '''Legal Standing & Estates''': In 1457, Sigrid and her husband, Dyre Erlendsson, conducted a high-level transaction with Knight Hartvig Krummedike at the estate of '''Sudreim in Hole (Ringerike)'''. While this estate is often c
2 CONC onfused with the Sudreim seat in Romerike, contemporary records prove that Sigrid’s allodial rights and influence were centered in the Ringerike region.
2 CONT * '''Social Status''': Her husband, Dyre Erlendsson, was the son of Erlend Baardsson and a key figure in the regional elite of Ringerike. The family’s high standing is further evidenced by the career of their son, '''Erlend Dyress
2 CONC on''', who in 1507 served on a prestigious judicial commission in Oslo alongside bishops and members of the Council of the Realm (Riksrådet) at the request of the future King Christian II.
2 CONT * '''The Holter Connection''': In 1490, Erlend Dyresson (Sigrid’s son) consolidated family holdings by purchasing ancestral lands in Rå (Norderhov) from his first cousin, Anders Amundsson (grandson of Jon Holteson). This transacti
2 CONC on definitively confirms Sigrid’s place within the Holter/Rå lineage, aligning with the reconstruction of the Holter family by Asgaut Steinnes (NST VIII, 1942).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources''':
2 CONT # DN VIII, No. 363 (1457): Record of Sigrid Jonsdatter and Dyre Erlendsson’s transaction at Sudreim (Ringerike).
2 CONT # DN XXI, No. 634 (1490): Land sale between Erlend Dyresson and his kinsman Anders Amundsson, son of Amund Jonsson Holter.
2 CONT # Oslo Rådstue (1507): Minutes of the judicial commission involving Erlend Dyresson and the high nobility.
2 CONT # Tore H. Vigerust: Skandinavisk Historisk Magazin - anmeldelse, Slekt og Data 1995, No. 3, p. 24-25.
2 CONT # Asgaut Steinnes: Mats-sønerne og ætta deira, NST VIII (1942), p. 305–349.
