2 CONT
2 CONT Since https://www.geni.com/people/Boris/6000000171494636930 is not able to add to this About, I have copied his remarks from the discussion about Åsa into her About (Remi Pedersen):
2 CONT
2 CONT "Since the "About" section of Åsa Ulvsdotter’s profile remains locked, I believe it is necessary to present the following evidence-based reconstruction here.
2 CONT
2 CONT The identity of Åsa Ulvsdotter (d. 1433) of Elingård is central to discussions of Norwegian noble continuity. This analysis synthesizes archival findings and legal precedents to justify her descent from Knight Ulf Holmgeirsson and
2 CONC  Cecilia Jonsdatter.
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Paternal Hypotheses: Ulf Jonsson (Roos) vs. Ulf Holmgeirsson (Lejonbalk)T. Vigerust’s hypothesis regarding Ulf Jonsson (Roos) was revised by him in 2003 [11] due to chronological flaws: Åsa’s brother, Arnstein Ulfsson, was acti
2 CONC ve by 1363 [13], making Ulf Jonsson’s (b. after 1332) paternity impossible.
2 CONT Ulf Holmgeirsson remains the only viable figure. SDHK No. 20683 (1426) confirms that his daughter, Katarina Ulvsdotter, officially approved her mother’s donation. This proves the existence of Cecilia Jonsdatter’s legitimate heirs 
2 CONC and validates her motherhood of Åsa.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. The Ulfsson Siblings and Chronological Seniority
2 CONT Ulf Holmgeirsson likely had two marriages. The elder children (Arnstein [4] and Ragnhild) belong to the first marriage. The younger group, born to Cecilia Jonsdatter after 1358, includes Åsa, Katarina, Amund, Olaf, and Karl [5].
2 CONT
2 CONT III. Landed Assets and the Hammarøy Legal Precedent
2 CONT Landed assets demonstrate a clear link to the Sudreim domain. Åsa held Elingård as allodial land (odel), which was legally restricted to legitimate kin. The 1431/32 litigation over Hammarøy [2] (Cecilia’s inheritance) involved Åsa
2 CONC ’s husband, son, and brother Olaf Ulfsson as legitimate co-heirs.
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. Historiographical Critique: Ulv Saxesson and the 1445 Diploma
2 CONT Ulv Saxesson died c. 1350 and could not be Åsa’s father. The 1445 diploma [6], often cited as proof of "extinction," merely reflects local Swedish interests at the time. It does not override the documented allodial rights exercise
2 CONC d by Åsa’s family in Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT V. Counter-arguments
2 CONT
2 CONT - Regarding "Childlessness": SDHK No. 20683 [3] definitively refutes this myth.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Lack of Direct Mention: In Norway, Allodial Law (Odelsrett) was the highest proof of kinship. Åsa’s possession of Elingård is the legal equivalent of a filiation record.
2 CONT
2 CONT The descent of Åsa Ulvsdotter from Ulf Holmgeirsson and Cecilia Jonsdatter is the most robust scientific model within the 15th-century legal framework.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources and Literature:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. DN I, No. 741/743 (1433) - Probate and division of Åsa Ulvsdotter's estate at Elingård.
2 CONT 2. DN XVI, No. 95 (1431/32) - Evidence of Åsa’s family rights and litigation regarding the island of Hammarøy.
2 CONT 3. SDHK No. 20683 (1426); SDHK No. 17559 (1410) - Legal acts of Katarina Ulvsdotter and Cecilia Jonsdatter (Proof of issue).
2 CONT 4. DN II, No. 649 (1419) - Documents regarding the disposal of Arnstein Ulfsson's inheritance.
2 CONT 5. DN I, No. 634; DN VI, No. 483; DN III, No. 721 - Records mentioning Karl Ulfsson and Olaf Ulfsson.
2 CONT 6. DN XVI, No. 151 (1445) - Confirmation of the Forsvik donation by collateral relatives (Roos family).
2 CONT 7. Gillingstam, H. Lejonbalk // Äldre Svenska Frälsesläkter (ÄSF). Stockholm, 1989.
2 CONT 8. Huitfeldt-Kaas, H. J. Sudrheim-ætten // Norsk Personalhistorisk Tidsskrift (NPT), 1885.
2 CONT 9. Løberg, L. Om Åsa Ulvsdotter og Elinættas mødrene opphav // Norsk Slektshistorisk Tidsskrift (NST), 2004. Vol. 39.
2 CONT 10. Vigerust, T. H. Discussion protocols and genealogical research (2001).
2 CONT 11. Digitalarkivets brukerforum. Post 16490 (Vigerust’s revision of the hypothesis, dated 09.08.2003).
2 CONT 12. Larsson, L.-O. Det medeltida Värend. Lund, 1964.
2 CONT 13. Lund, A. Hustru Sigrid Ansteinsdatter og Holte-sønnenes ætt. 1951."
