2 CONT General Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT Virgin Agnes was King Håkon V.'s eldest daughter. Her mother is not known. She was engaged to Mr. Havtore in 1302. (Isl. Ann. IV, V). At that time she was hardly much more than 10 years old. The marriage between them can therefore
2 CONC  only have been entered into several years later, probably around 1307. In dowry with the wife, Mr. Havtore by King Håkon 15 smaller farms on Romerike, but the king revoked this disposition. Instead, he donated 6 markebol in Sorkn
2 CONC es in Solør to hr. Havtore and Mrs. Agnes, presumably this whole farm. The diploma is dated Bergen 09.01.1312 (DN I 132): From, Volume III 1301-1319, no. 756:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information:
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes married Havtore Jonsson Roos til Sudreim, son of Jon Raud Ivarsson Roos til Sudreim and Unknown, in 1302. (Havtore Jonsson Roos til Sudreim was born circa 1275 and died in 1320 in Sørum (Sudreim, Skedjuhof)), Sørum, Akershus
2 CONC , Norway .)
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes married Havtore Jonsson Roos Til Sudreim, son of Jon Raud Ivarsson Roos Til Sudreim and Ukjent, in 1302. (Havtore Jonsson Roos Til Sudreim was born around 1275 and died in 1320 in Sørum (Sudreim, Skedjuhof)), Sørum, Akershus
2 CONC  , Norway.)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes was the illegitimate daughter of Håkan V Magnusson, the last of the Sverreätten and her sons had inheritance rights to the Norwegian throne. She was married to Councilor Hafthor Jo
