2 NOTE Galtarætt i Grimsnesi page 304. Arnason has shown no. 13 - "Onefnd dottir Håkonar Jonssonar" - (unknown daughter of Håkon Jonsson). Under no. 14 Håkon Jonsson, Arnason goes on to tell a "oliklega sögn" - (an improbable story) from
3 CONC  Icelandic "erfdasögnum" ("oral story inheritance"). The story according to Arnason claimed -in short- that Håkon Jonsson was married twice - and that Norwegian genealogists were wrong to claim that Håkon was childless. The story 
3 CONC seems to claim Magnus Håkonsson (Lagabøte?) as his son as the rose seal was supposed to be used by both.     
