2 CONT A. Y. Cheyne, The Cheyne Family, stated that Thomas Chene of Straloch (2216) acted as procurator for Robert Chene of Tullidask (4114), in 1560 [Aberd. Sheriff Court Vol. II. Diet. 18. 6.1560.]. The parentage of Robert Cheyne of Tu
2 CONC llidask (Tilliedesk perhaps?) is not known.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Cheyne 7th of Essilmont died about 1564 in Shetland Islands, Scotland. Thomas Cheyne, 7th of Essilmont, probably died in 1564. His son Patrick inherited his land in Shetland in September and October of that year.2,5
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Patrick Cheyne, knight, of Essilmont was mentioned in an abstracted entry on the The Commissarint Record of Edinburgh. Register of Testaments. First Section--1514-1600, probably at the death of his father, Thomas Cheyne, feur,
2 CONC  of Essilmont, whose entry was dated 27 July 1565. The entry reads: "Cheyne (Chayne), Sir Patrick, knight, of Essilmonth 18 Jul 1565 and Cheyne (Chayne), Thomas, fear, of Essilmonthe 27 Jul 1565".6
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Cheyne of Essilmont was mentioned in Aberdeen Birth Briefs. The entry has to do with the ancestry of his great-grandson Gilbert Chalmer, Burgess of Aberdeen.7
