1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cay von Pogwisch (or Kay Powisch as the military records call him) served in the Danish army for 42 years and fought in some of Denmark's most important battles. He was wounded in the Battle of Lund in 1676, as was
2 CONC  two of his brothers, and one of them later died. In the 1680s he served in the 2nd Jutland Regiment under Erasmus Casimir von Bahsen, first as Lieutenant under Captain (ritmester) Peter Stensen and later as Captain (ritmester) hi
2 CONC mself. According to a letter from his wife, he also served in the Danish auxiliaries that were sent to Flanders and Ireland but upon his return, he was forced to retire because of a disagreement with Lieutenant General Pless. 
