1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Han var først gift med Ambjørg Halvorsdtr. Nordal. Barn: Halvor (til Hørte), Maren (g.m. Rasmus Hansen Solberg), Kari (g.m. Ole Bjørnsen Solberg). Så giftet han seg med Siri Torgersdtr. Holtsmark, f. ca. 1628, d. 1
2 CONC 695. Barn: Ambjørg (g.m. Paul Hansen Røer, Nesodden), Maren (g.m. Hans Hansen Røer d.e. - se nedenfor), Marte (g.m. I Hans Hansen Røer d.y.; g.m. II Herman Helgesen Holter, Nes, Romerike -til Sjåstad).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Sten (ca.1619 - 1688) was the son of Oluf Stensen Søndre Horn in Lier and Anne Kjellsdatter Tordenstjerne (died 1645). Sten Olufsen was once married to Ambjørg Halvorsdatter Nordal. Twice he was married to Siri Torgersdatter Holts
2 CONC mark (1628 - 1695) (mother of Marte) Sten used the farm Nordal until he took over the father's farm Hon. Of the stolen land, he owned the outer Mørk in Lier, Skjellestad in Asker and Valle in Onsøy. He is also listed from 1650 wit
2 CONC h 9 1/2 lp. in Nordre Horn, which he at this time used as an underuse. He later became the sole owner of this farm Horn. Sten also owned a share in southern Bergskog. From no later than 1668 he used Vefsrud under Horn. He received
2 CONC  a royal deed at Vefsrud for 31 dlr. 1 place in 1672. Son-in-law Han Hansen Røer (the elder) from Nesodden.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Søndre Horn is mentioned in 1593/94 Alf. By 1604, I) Nils, mentioned until 1636, took over. The owner, II) Oluf Stensen Rolsrud, Eiker, apparently did not move here until 1640 (according to the book about the genus Røer - Røhr 
2 CONC by PK Røhr, Kristiania 1920). His parents were Sten Olufsen Skjellestad in Asker (son of Oluf Vaker in Norderhov) and ... Nilsdtr., B. Nordal. Oluf was married to Anne Kjellsdtr.  Kjell Lauritssen to Hanevoll in Skoger, who was th
2 CONC e son of Laurits Nilsen to StensHorne in Eiker). Children: Kjell, Marte (gm Peder Christensen Satte), Sten. In 1624, on the occasion of the change of spouse (see owners), an inspection had been held on the farm. There were no othe
2 CONC r houses than an old stable, a rotten cattle house and two barns. The upper barn was dilapidated. A stable had also been built for the western barn. The seed is stated to be 3 barrels 2 settings. 40 loads of hay could be harvested
2 CONC . In a stream on the farm there was an old rotten saw and an old mill noise. There was spruce forest for the farm, including some sawn timber. Oluf Stensen also became the owner of Nordre Horn - by 1637. In addition, he owned 1 ¼ 
2 CONC skpd. i Saue i Lier, 1 ½ skpd. in Vinsvoll in Eiker and 17 ½ lp. in Rolsrud. Oluf died in the early 1640s, while Anne lived until 1645.
2 CONT Then the son III) Sten Olufsen, born in 1619 and died in 1688. He was first married to Ambjørg Halvorsdtr. Nordal. Children: Halvor (to Hørte), Maren (gm Rasmus Hansen Solberg), Kari (gm Ole Bjørnsen Solberg). Then he married Siri
2 CONC  Torgersdtr. Holtsmark, born in 1628 and died in 1695. Sten and Siri children. 1. Ambjørg she married Paul Hansen  Røer. 2. Maren married Hans Hansen Røer. 3. Marte married twice (1) Hans Hansen, then she married (2) Herman Helges
2 CONC en Holter. Sten used Nordal until he took over his father's farm. Of the land, he owned Ytre Mørk in Lier, Skjellestad in Asker and Valle in Onsøy. In addition, he is listed from 1650 with 9 ½ lp. in Nordre Horn, which he at this 
2 CONC time used as an underuse. Later he also became the sole owner of this Horn farm. Sten also owned a share in Søndre Berskog. From no later than 1668 he used Vefsrud under Horn. He received a royal deed at Vefsrud for 31 dlr. 1 ort 
2 CONC in 1672. Bård Gunnerud and Sven Kopperud were in 1666 convicted of assault on Sten, who received a compensation of 15 dlr.
2 CONT Hans Hansen Røer was born in 1661 and he died in 1737. He married Maren Stensdatter  Horn she was born in 1664 and she died in 1715. Hans and Maren children. 1.  Stenber Hanssen, Hans Hanssen, Sten Hanssen, Siri Hansdotter married
2 CONC  Anders Andersen, Mari Hansdotter married Nils Svensen, Paul Hanssen, Peder Hanssen. Han Hansen Roer was the son of Hans Paulsen Røer and Maren Christoffersdatter. Hans was born in Dahl in Frogn. He redeemed the co-owners of Horn 
2 CONC by change of spouse in 1693 and 1694 and by deed of 1697. At the change after Maren in 1715, both the gross and net assets were barely 674 dlr., As the change costs were paid with ready money without expenses in the estate. They o
2 CONC wned estates in the following farms, besides Horn with Vefsrud: Nordre Hørte, Nordre Sylling, Pilterud in Modum and Kimmerud in Modum. The livestock consisted of 4 horses, of which 1 dragon horse, 25 cattle, 16 sheep, 15 goats and
2 CONC  9 pigs. Two mill houses, the upper and the lower, were assessed at 4 and 3 dlr, respectively. 1200 spruce table had a total value of 72 dlr. Of silverware, worth about 75 dlr., There was 1 jug with lion feet, weight 48, 2 smaller
2 CONC  jugs, 2 cups and a lot of spoons. Almost everything was provided with inscriptions, i.a. Hans Hansen and Maren Steensdatter and the years 1697, 1689 and 1685, Povel Hansen, Povel Simensen 1690, Svend Povelsen 1661, Marthe Steensd
2 CONC atter 1690, TESHHSR 1689, Hans Hansen 1690, SOSAHD 1657, HSS 1663, Jahn von Cappelen and Otto von Cappelen 1690. There were also books, namely a house and travel bible, "Naadens Aandelig Marcketz tiid" and a small prayer book with
2 CONC  a white parchment binding. A small liquor boiler with a hat and pipe was valued at just over 3 dlr. Otherwise, contents and chattels are registered in the realm sample. Finally, a Flemish rug "woven by King Salmon" can be mention
2 CONC ed here. When Hans died, the son took over.
2 CONT Hans Hansen was born in 1696 and he died in 1763.  He married his cousin Helle Hermansdatter, she was born in 1703 and she died in 1773. Hans and Helle children were. Hans Hansen, Mari Hansdotter, she lived in Romerike in 1773, sh
2 CONC e never married, Herman Hansen, Marte Hansdotter married twice. (1) widow Christoffer Larsen Enger, then she married (2) widow Truls Narvesen Solberg, Margarete Hansdotter married Asle Guttormsen from Askerud, Modum. In 1723 Hans 
2 CONC received a deed of 3 lp. in Horn by some party owners. Hans was a farmer on Øren on Åssida from 1727, but later moved to Fure in Modum, where he lived after his father's death. In 1739 he received a deed to 7 heirs in the farm. Th
2 CONC e price of each brother ticket was 160 dlr. and on each sister lot 80 dlr. Hans issued a mortgage bond of 800 dlr. in 1739. Five years later he borrowed 1160 dlr. In 1752, half of the farm was taken over for 800 dlr. of the eldest
2 CONC  son. Hans they took a mortgage loan of 600 dlr. the year after. In 1757 he bought a small inheritance from Hans Rasmussen Nordal.
2 CONT The co-user was the son Hans Hansen, born in 1720 and he died in 1797. He was first married to Berte Olsdatter from Vardal, Sande. She was born in 1726 and died in 1773 Hans and Berte children were. Helle Hansdotter married Asle T
2 CONC rulsen Dignes, Modum, Dorthea  Hansdotter married Åke Larsen Hegg, Jan Hanssen, Hans Hanssen,Margrete (Grete) Hansdotter married twice. (1) Simon Bentsen Holtsmark, (2) then widower Anders Hansen Eik, Marte Marie Hansdotter marrie
2 CONC d Lars Trulsen Solberg, Ole Hanssen died young. Then Hans married widow Randi Mathiasdatter, she was boorn in 1728. Her parents were sheriff Mathias Knutsen Sass in Modum and wife Boel Jensdatter. Randi was the mother of Anne Mari
2 CONC e Hansdotter Køster who married Hans Christoffersen Skjæret. Hans took a mortgage loan of 500 dlr. in 1753, and repaid the debt with an equal loan in 1764. In 1769 he received a deed to the rest of the farm for 1400 dlr. of his mo
2 CONC ther. In the event of a change of cousin after Berte Olsdtr. in 1775 the gross fortune was 4800 dlr. and the net worth 2500 dlr. Hans distributed 1500 dlr. to the children and bore all the expenses of the shift itself. He immediat
2 CONC ely issued a bond of 1000 dlr. with 1st prior. mortgage in one half and 2nd prior. mortgage in the other half of the farm. The following year he handed over one half for 1800 dlr. to his eldest son. Later that year, Hans received 
2 CONC a deed to three heirs' heirs in Horn, for a total of 350 dlr. At the same time, he issued a 2nd prior. mortgage bond of 750 dlr. to his benefactors Hans, Ole and Marte Marie. In 1780, his son Hans sold his inheritance from his mot
2 CONC her for 300 dlr. to his father. His they took the same year 1st-prior. mortgage of 500 dlr., which he increased by 600 dlr. just after. In 1785 he then repaid the debt by borrowing 1700 dlr., and two years later he borrowed 495 dl
