2 CONT Hans Hanssen son Jan Hansen took over the farm.  Jan was born in 1755 and he died in 1807.  Jan Hansen married Tolline Ottersdatter,  she was born in 1756 and she died in 1835. Jan Hansen and Tolline children were. Hans Hanssen, O
2 CONC tter Hanssen, Berte Marie Hansdotter, she married Ole Aslesen, Ole Hanssen, Dorte Hansdotter married Oven Christoffersen Onstad.Jan Hanssen borrowed 1250 dlr. in 1776, and repaid the debt with a loan of 900 dlr. in 1779. In 1802 h
2 CONC e mortgaged the property for 2990 dlr. to merchant Hans Enger in Kristiania. By agreement, no interest was to be paid on the loan. Then the farm was divided into two equal parts. As mentioned, in 1776 he had given up half of the f
2 CONC arm, and in 1790 he also left the last half to his eldest son. Hans had at this time a total debt burden of approx. 4380 dlr. When Jan died he owned two parts of the farm.  The first part went to his son Ole Jansen.
2 CONT Ole Jansen was born in 1789 and he died in 1864.  Ole married his cousin Berte Simonsdatter, she was born in 1786 and she died in 1869. Ole and Berte children were. Grete Olsdotter, Randi Johanne Olsdotter, Grete Dorthea Olsdotter
2 CONC , she married goldsmith Anders Olsen, Sille Olsdotter, Tolline Olsdotter and Jan Olson, Bent Olsson. He probably used this part in 1808, the same year he got a purchase contract for the other half of the farm from his brother Hans
