1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Arild Hake''', d.æ.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rådmand i København.
2 CONT
2 CONT Link:
2 CONT * https://finnholbek.dk/getperson.php?personID=I78482&tree=2
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Arild Hake born about 1527 and deceased 26 October 1590 (Friday) - København, Sjælland, Danmark, aged about 63 years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father:: Arild Hake ca 1470.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://gw.geneanet.org/brynjulf?lang=en&n=hake&oc=1&p=arild
2 CONT
2 CONT Hake, or Hakes, is a surname of English and Nordic origin, with Hakes being patronymic from Hake (Hakeson/Hakesonn). The origins of Hake(s) are said to derive from the Old Norse word haki, which is cognate with the word 'hook' and
2 CONC  given originally to someone in the fishing trade.
2 CONT
2 CONT The surname also derives from the Northern Germanic surname Haack, which is a name from Middle Low German hake (English: young fellow). The surname was first recorded in the eastern counties of England and originated under the pre
2 CONC -9th century Danish-Norwegian Viking influence.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hake_(surname)
