2 CONT !SOURCE: GEDCOM: 1996 from Carolyn Bartholomew, Modesto, CA, used AG Jeffrey Svare Rec has after given and surname, Farm Name of GYLDENAAR. SOURCE:: fam rec Beryl E. Lewis; later, 1992, added from pedigree ch of Carolyn Cain Batho
2 CONC lomew, Modesto, CA. Article in HEDMARKS SLEKTSCHISTORIELAGS TIDSSKRIFT, "Dyre Sevaldsens sleft og dens aettlinger pa Store Re i Stange og Gaustad i Romedal" by Asbjorn Hagen-Bergseng, 1944.  It outlines the family from Dyre Mogens
2 CONC en and Mette Rasmusdatter Hiorth back to Erland Bardsen. The family assumed the Gyldenaar as part of their ascension into the nobility. It is not a farm name.  Not all members of the family used it evidently.  Refer to the article
2 CONC .
2 CONT === BIRTH: Abt 1546 (IGI states Abt 1542) MA ===
2 CONT BIRTH: Abt 1546 (IGI states Abt 1542) MARRIAGE:  IGI for SS.  The IGI sates marriage was 1589 in Stange, Hedmark, Norway. ORDINANCES:IGI for B, E, & SP - Film #453853.  SP from temple ordinance card.  The sealer noticed that Dyre'
2 CONC s last name is spelled differently than the parents.  This probably was my mistake (Barbara Christenson) in typing, The sealer affirmed that the sealing was true regardless of the spelling.  In checking later the IGI under the Gyl
2 CONC denaar spelling, the sealing had been done 3 Oct 1961.  I am changing the spelling from Glydenaar back to Gyldenaar. PROFESSIONAL RESEARCH:  Hedmark slekts historielage tidsskrift 1.  Norsk Tidsskrift for Genealogi 1,b.2,p. 265 2,
2 CONC  p. 260   3, p. 243  Research by: Mrs. Alfhild Gundersen Soren Jaabeksgt.8.7. Oslo 4. Norway SUPPORTING FAMILY RECORDS: Family group sheet with dates stamped by temple workers plus added paper  with sealer, witness, and proxy name
2 CONC s. In possession of: Barbara Christenson, Provo, Utah 84604. Verna's Book: 75
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT Gyldenaar is not a place but a nobility name.
